GitHub Actions Events & Triggers

Today I learned how events and triggers decide when a GitHub Actions workflow should run.

🔹 push
Triggers a workflow when code is pushed to a branch.
 Commonly used for:
Build
Test
Lint checks

🔹 pull_request
Runs workflows on PR actions like open or update.
 Helps in:
Code quality checks
Validation before merge

🔹 workflow_dispatch
Allows manual execution of workflows.
 Useful for:
On-demand deployments
Manual testing pipelines

🔹 schedule
Runs workflows on a cron-based schedule.
 Used for:
Nightly builds
Periodic scans

🔥 3-Line Takeaway
Events control execution.
 Triggers automate timing.
 CI/CD starts with actions.
